module display_generic.pos_1

// A GENERIC INSTANCE IN A SLOT (274.7 B1b-3): `Vec[int]` printed through the
// `@display` the SHELL carries, not through anything novac emits itself.
//
// THREE ELEMENTS AND NOT ONE, deliberately: the separator between them is part
// of the form std's own example asserts (`collections/vec/protocols.nv:192`
// gives `"Vec[1, 2, 3]"`), and a one-element vector keeps a shape that never
// prints a separator at all.
//
// WHY THIS IS THE ONE GENERIC THAT WORKS TODAY, and the fixture says it so the
// next reader does not try the others and conclude the wave is broken. An
// instance method reaches novac only through the shell's interop surface, and
// the surface is whatever the probe kept alive. Measured 2026-09-18 after the
// probe was grown: the shell defines `Vec____nova_int_method_display`, which is
// exactly the name `instance_body` builds for a RECORD head -- while
// `NovaOpt_*_method_display` and `NovaRes_*_method_display` are absent
// entirely, and novac could not spell them anyway (`instance_body` ices on a
// generic SUM by design). So `Option` and `Result` stay refused, by name, and
// that refusal is asserted in `neg_1` beside this file.

fn main() {
    ro v = []int.of(1, 2, 3)
    println("${v}")
}
